---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Privacy Notice | DAT Construction" description="Privacy notice compliant with India's Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023.">
  <div class="page-banner">
    <div class="section-container">
      <div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> <span>/</span> <strong>Privacy Notice</strong></div>
      <h1>Privacy Notice</h1>
      <p class="banner-sub">Information handling, data collection, and grievance policy under India's Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-container legal-content">
      <h2>1. Overview & Data Fiduciary</h2>
      <p>DAT Construction ("Company", "We") respects your privacy. This privacy notice explains how we collect, store, process, and protect personal data submitted via our enquiry forms in compliance with the Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act 2023 of India.</p>

      <h2>2. Data Collected</h2>
      <p>When you submit an enquiry on our website, we collect the following personal data:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Full Name:</strong> To identify you and address your enquiry.</li>
        <li><strong>Phone Number:</strong> To contact you regarding project scope, site details, or BOQ estimates.</li>
        <li><strong>Email Address:</strong> To send formal quotations and technical documents.</li>
        <li><strong>Project & Scope Details:</strong> Information provided in the message box describing site location, timeline, and requirements.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Purpose of Processing</h2>
      <p>Personal data is processed strictly for the following purpose(s):</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Evaluating project requirements and communicating quotations.</li>
        <li>Fulfilling pre-contractual and statutory inquiries for civil engineering services.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>We retain personal data only for as long as necessary to fulfill the enquiry purpose or to comply with applicable statutory legal and audit obligations in India.</p>

      <h2>5. Your Rights</h2>
      <p>Under the DPDP Act 2023, you have the right to request access, correction, updating, or erasure of your personal data held by us, or to withdraw your consent for processing.</p>

      <h2>6. Grievance Officer & Data Contact</h2>
      <p>If you have any questions, concerns, or grievances regarding your personal data, please contact our designated Grievance Officer:</p>
      <div class="contact-card">
        <strong>Office Address:</strong> 7/C, Rajendra Nagar, Indore, Madhya Pradesh - 452012, India
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal-content {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background-color: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    padding: 40px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }
  .legal-content h2 {
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    color: var(--navy-deep);
    margin: 28px 0 12px;
  }
  .legal-content h2:first-of-type {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .legal-content p, .legal-content ul {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .legal-content ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  .contact-card {
    background-color: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-color);
    padding: 20px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
